<p>The intake call is where most of the real work happens, and it's deliberately not a checklist.</p>

<p>For an <strong>accounting practice</strong>, that means walking through how a new client actually gets onboarded, where FICA and SARS documentation sits, how month-end reporting gets assembled, and who chases outstanding information and how.</p>

<figure class="article-inline-img">
  <img src="/images/article-audit-sage.png" alt="A six-person accounting practice loses roughly R234,000 a year to three hours of manual admin per staff member per week, at a R1,500 chargeable rate" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
